Literature sweep completed 2026-05-04.

Effector identification:
- PWT7 is an avirulence effector from Pyricularia oryzae (Avena/Lolium blast
  pathotypes; isolate Br58). Cloned by Asuke et al. 2023 MPMI (gene F38).
  98 aa precursor; signal peptide 1-20; mature chain 21-98 = 78 residues.
  Full precursor sequence: MQFGYLFALA TAFGIATPVM ARRCVVEMVG RDGTFEFVND
  KEYCVPPEPM LQFGQKTDLR PKKPGYKFFV NVDAGCTTAV HVKGKMPKGY FFRTRWEN
  Three cysteines (C24, C44, C76 precursor). No public UniProt accession.
  DDBJ project accessions PRJDB14584/PRJDB14749 (Asuke 2023).
- MAX fold confirmed by structural context (crystallized with Rwt7-HMA at 1.6 Å
  and 0.99 Å; Yu 2025). Not explicitly classified as MAX in Asuke 2023 by sequence.
- Alleles: PWT7Ele (1 aa diff), PWT7LomE (1 aa diff from Ele), PWT7Lom (4 aa diff),
  PWT7Set (4 aa diff) — all functional except TP2 which is suppressed.

Source PDB and numbering convention:
- Chain A: AF3 monomer of Pikp-1 HMA (UniProt E9KPB5, residues 186-263),
  renumbered 1-78 (pipeline = literature - 185). Shared with all pikp1_* campaigns.
- Chain B: 9TFP chain B (PWT7; Rwt7-HMA/PWT7 crystal structure, 1.6 Å;
  Yu et al. 2025; HPUB — Banfield lab data). Request access from M.J. Banfield.
  Working assumption: precursor numbering. Verify N39 = binding-critical Asn.
  Alternative higher-res source: 9TFT chain B (0.99 Å; same depositors).
- Complex template: 9TFP (cross-system alignment; superpose AF3 Pikp-1 HMA onto
  Rwt7-HMA from 9TFP). 6G10 is NOT used.

Binding face determination (CONFIRMED — campaign-specific):
- PWT7 binds Rwt7-HMA at the N-terminal β1/M1 face: M1 of Rwt7-HMA forms
  extensive interactions with PWT7; interface spans "two faces" of Rwt7-HMA;
  central contacts are N39 and D40 of PWT7 (precursor numbering = N19/D20 mature
  = β2 of PWT7 MAX fold).
- M1 of Rwt7-HMA = pipeline position 1 of Pikp-1 HMA (= Lys-186).
- This is the OPPOSITE END of the HMA from the canonical AVR-Pik binding face
  (β4/C-tail = pipeline ~67-78).
- Distinct from all other sibling campaigns: avrpikf uses β4 (pipeline 67-78),
  avrpia uses α1/β2 (pipeline 19-42), pby2 uses β3 (pipeline 43-49).
- The β1/N-terminal region (pipeline 1-30) was ANCHORED in all sibling campaigns
  but is the PRIMARY REDESIGN TARGET in this campaign.
- Binding-critical: N39R in PWT7 abolishes binding (Yu 2025). KD = 2.92 nM.

Primary contig:
  15-28/A31-78 B
  (Flex: pipeline 1-30, native 30 residues; Anchor: pipeline 31-78)

Campaign-blockers: None. 9TFP (Banfield lab data) is the structural basis; user
has access. No further literature gap.

Primary papers cited:
- Asuke et al. 2023 MPMI (PWT7 cloning, sequence, gene structure, alleles)
- Yu et al. 2025 bioRxiv (9TFP structure; Rwt7-HMA/PWT7 binding face; N39R;
  KD = 2.92 nM; "two faces" binding mode)
- Asuke et al. 2025 bioRxiv (PWT7 biology; Rwt7 TKP; distribution MoE/MoL)
- Maqbool 2015 eLife (Pikp-1 HMA scaffold)
- De la Concepcion 2018 Nat Plants (HMA Interface 1/2/3 definition)
- Guo 2018 PNAS (distinct HMA binding faces; comparison with AVR-Pia)
- Varden 2019 JBC (AVR-Pia face; for contrast)

